Strong Final Interview Answer

Snowflake Virtual Warehouses support three states: STARTED, SUSPENDED, and RESIZING. Started warehouses actively process queries and consume credits, while suspended warehouses consume no credits because compute nodes are shut down. Warehouses can automatically suspend after inactivity using the AUTO_SUSPEND parameter and automatically resume using AUTO_RESUME. Snowflake also supports INITIALLY_SUSPENDED to prevent immediate billing after creation. A key performance consideration is that warehouse cache is cleared during suspension, which may cause slower query performance after resume due to cold cache effects.
